% An overflow under negation must not turn into an affirmative answer: were
% the binding merely dropped, blocked(a) would be underived and allowed(a)
% derived, which the program, read over the integers, denies.  The
% evaluation fails instead, and allowed(a) is never printed.
score(a, 9223372036854775807). score(b, 5).

blocked(X) :- score(X, S), S + 1 > 100.
allowed(X) :- score(X, _), not blocked(X).

allowed(X)?
